## A. Eight dispositions

| Finding | Verdict | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Training loader boundary | **PARTIAL** | The four named scripts now use `read_jsonl`, but three other training consumers still bypass it: [RF probe](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rq1_3_rf_probe.py:175), [continuation diagnostic](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/diagnose_continuation_effect.py:127), and [typed-decision trainer](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/train_typed_decision.py:52). The [guide’s complete-coverage claim](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:323) is premature. |
| Unsafe resume | **PARTIAL** | [The guard](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/generate_dataset_longhorizon.py:78) rejects a single incompatible stamp pair, including an unstamped legacy file. It does not compare generation configuration; a same-stamp resume with changed horizon or utility settings can append incompatible records. Mixed legacy/current stamps also trigger a `TypeError` while formatting the refusal message. |
| Single-family NaN | **ADDRESSED** | The [df=0 branch](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:186) returns null statistics, the [verdict logic](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_meta_config_grid.py:351) handles them, and the refreshed deep-arm JSON parses with strict rejection of NaN. |
| Replica indexing | **ADDRESSED** | [Guide §5.5.1](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:401) and [PROGRESS](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:737) state replicas 0–1 versus 2–3, with 4 unused. |
| Primary-null wording | **PARTIAL** | The report’s model text now names standardized slopes, but its [explicit `H0_slope` bullet](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_GRID.md:48) still says `b₁ = … = b_F`. The script and artifact specify equality of `b_f / sd_ref(f)`. |
| Version-bump rule | **ADDRESSED** | The [module docstring](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/versioning.py:5) now matches guide §6.6. |
| Honesty wording | **PARTIAL** | The main guide discussion and grid §6.3 now give the point estimate and CI, but “effect at most” remains in the [screen abstract](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_SCREEN.md:18), [screen §6](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_SCREEN.md:128), [grid abstract](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_META_CONFIG_GRID.md:24), and [guide ledger](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:634). |
| Stale p and half-width ratios | **ADDRESSED** | Grid §6.4 gives `4.9×10⁻⁴`; the artifact gives `0.000486246`. Screen §5 gives `1.65–1.77×`; recalculation from its artifact gives `1.689–1.766×`. |

I also recomputed the grid homogeneity statistic from serialized family slopes and joint-bootstrap SEs: χ² = **20.0587**, I² = **0.8006**.

## B. New-issue check — findings

- **[BLOCKER]** [train_typed_decision.py:52](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/train_typed_decision.py:52), [exp_rq1_3_rf_probe.py:175](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_rq1_3_rf_probe.py:175), [diagnose_continuation_effect.py:127](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/diagnose_continuation_effect.py:127): all feed training from unchecked JSONL reads. **Fix:** migrate all three to `read_jsonl` with explicit policy, then correct the guide’s coverage claim.
- **[MAJOR]** [exp_geartrain_transfer_probe.py:104](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/exp_geartrain_transfer_probe.py:104): the unconditional transfer note activates a recorded cross-version opt-in, although the two current files have the same raw stamps and the note gives no same-data A/B justification. Future mismatched files would pass. **Fix:** check without an opt-in by default; permit a note only for a justified same-data A/B comparison.
- **[MAJOR]** [generate_dataset_longhorizon.py:220](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/generate_dataset_longhorizon.py:220): `--resume` checks stamps but can append records generated with different same-version settings. **Fix:** compare the existing generation configuration with the requested configuration before copying or appending.
- **[MINOR]** [generate_dataset_longhorizon.py:90](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/scripts/generate_dataset_longhorizon.py:90): sorting mixed `(None, …)` and string stamp tuples raises `TypeError` instead of the promised guided `SystemExit`. **Fix:** format or sort stamp pairs using string representations.

## C. Merge readiness

**REVISE.** The refreshed statistics and most targeted corrections check out, but the standing specification still claims a complete training loader boundary that three scripts bypass. The resume configuration gap and contradictory normative and effect wording also need correction before the closing approval. This was a read-only audit; no tests or training were run.

VERDICT: REVISE
